# Comments
- ALWAYS Write comments and code in english, even if developers are french.

# Naming Conventions
- React component files: PascalCase (e.g., TestStep.tsx)
- Utility files: camelCase (e.g., createConnection.ts)
- Folders: camelCase for standard folders (e.g., utils), PascalCase for components (e.g., Logo)
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase with descriptive suffix (e.g., ResultData, TestType)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., SHOP_TEST_OPE_ID)

# Styles and CSS
- MANDATORY: Use CSS Modules with the classNameModule utility
- Name style files with the .module.scss suffix
- Main class names should be in PascalCase
- Modifiers and states should be in camelCase
- Avoid global styles unless necessary

# Typescript Typing
- Always type component props, if there is at least one prop, in a type defined juste before the component. For example :
```tsx
type ComponentProps = {
    name:string
}

const Component = ({ name }: ComponentProps) => {}
```

- Avoid any whenever possible, prefer specific types
- Create types/interfaces for structured data
- Use enums for predefined types

# React Components

- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use "use client" only when necessary
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks
- Pass data between steps via props
- Use the "handleNext" pattern for navigation between steps

